# dev/tasks is a directory junction (Windows) / symlink into the PRIVATE
# kitaekatt/tasks repo, where this project's task folders live and are
# version-controlled -- see "Task folders live in a private tasks repo" in
# CLAUDE.md. This entry is load-bearing: it is what stops git traversing the
# link and staging private task content into this PUBLIC repo. Do not add a
# !dev/tasks exception.
#
# BOTH forms are required. The trailing-slash form matches a DIRECTORY, which
# is what the link is on Windows (a junction). On macOS/Linux the link is a
# symlink, which git treats as a FILE, and a trailing-slash pattern never
# matches a file -- so without the bare form the entry silently fails open
# there and `git add -A` would stage the symlink (a machine-specific absolute
# path) into this public repo.
dev/tasks
dev/tasks/

